-- MAGIC     <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC         <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC         <div>
-- MAGIC             <strong style="color: #0d47a1; font-size: 1.1em;">Key Considerations</strong>
-- MAGIC             <ul>
-- MAGIC               <li>Potential temporary disruption during migration.</li>
-- MAGIC               <li>All metadata, permissions, and objects move in a single wave.</li>
-- MAGIC               <li>Validate workloads and permissions post-migration.</li>
-- MAGIC               <li>Best for workspaces with limited complexity, minimal legacy workloads, or when there’s a desire for a rapid cutover.</li>
-- MAGIC             </ul>
-- MAGIC         </div>
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC </div>

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A1. Overall Process
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Run the UCX tool to assess migration readiness.
-- MAGIC 1. Use migration scripts/automated tools to convert HMS tables/views/functions to UC equivalents (register external tables, re-grant privileges).
-- MAGIC 1. Refactor workloads
-- MAGIC    - Update all jobs, notebooks, dashboards, and pipelines to use the new UC naming convention (catalog.schema.table).

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ## B. Parallel Migration
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Using this approach, we set up a new, dedicated, UC-enabled workspace alongside the legacy HMS workspace, migrating artifacts and workloads gradually.
-- MAGIC
